                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "There is some alright and a lot bad about this game. I think the biggest problem I have here is that it's essentially a knock-off of Crimsonland - almost all of the weapons, abilities, and creatures are basically either the same or slightly altered versions from Crimsonland, and with such blatant plagiarism I can't in good conscience recommend this game. \n\n Re-skin aside, the gameplay is a mixture of okay with awful. The controls are just so frustratingly awful and you spend the entire game fighting the mouse as anytime you move near an edge of the screen it stays in place rather than following your character, meaning that every time you move (which is at almost all times) your aim is thrown off and constantly needs to be corrected. Even when you aren't near the edge moving your mouse is just awful, I had to max out the games sensitivity and my mouses dpi just to properly aim but at the risk of the reticle randomly stopping or slowing depending on my characters movement and throwing off the accuracy even further. \n\nBalancing is just completely off, with some weapons being ludicrously underpowered compared to others with no logical reasoning for it. Also, spiders are just crazily overpowered and completely nullify the threat of almost every other creature in comparison. This wouldn't be a problem if they weren't so damn common, appearing mere moments into the game and persisting throughout becoming even more of a killing machine once they get lasers. On the other hand, zombies are pathetic and you can easily maneuver through hordes of them with ease, and the only use they serve as is xp and buffers between your bullets and the spiders.\n\nAnother thing that is problematic is the description for skills. They are very vague and so many of them seem to have little to no effect that it is hard to tell how much they have actually changed your stats, while others are obviously superior and make a noticeable difference. This just adds to an overall imbalanced game. Something I admit that is unique compared to Crimsonland is the secondary weapons, which offer powerful abilites on top of the pickups, weapons, and perks you already have. These however suffer the same problem as the other weapons in the game in being completely unbalanced, with several of them completely useless compared to others, or having a side effect that makes them a bad choice such as in the case of the missile launcher where it slows you down and makes turning even slower making it a death sentence to use should any creatures be to the side of or behind you (which is exactly where the spider ai is trying to get to).\n\nIn conclusion the game is an unbalanced mess with awful controls that is essentially the equivalent of a middle-schooler copying an article off of wikipedia for an essay and editing a couple of sentences before turning it in. While the dev does seem to be listening to some of the reviews and forums, this game needs a hell of a lot of work and originality before it actually becomes a good game. 3.5/10",
